## Interview Definition

Ansible is an open-source, agentless automation and configuration management tool that uses SSH to manage multiple servers from a central control node. It automates software installation, configuration management, application deployment, server provisioning, and administrative tasks through YAML-based playbooks.

### One-Line Definition

Ansible is a tool that automates repetitive server administration and infrastructure management tasks across multiple systems from a single control node.
